      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks. The precedent part is probably our best bet. One specific thing that's causing a headache is the \"encroachment\" clause. It's written in a way that suggests even minor structural encroachments from neighbor properties could potentially invalidate the variance for the whole parcel, even if they aren't part of the new development. It feels a bit like the code is treating these small boundary overlaps as a massive violation. How should I frame the argument to the zoning board to minimize the impact of these existing encroachments on our application?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
